# Source requirements for the Cosmos 3 reasoner serving venv (Python 3.12).
# vllm>=0.23.0 is the load-bearing floor: the first vLLM release line that
# serves the Cosmos 3 reasoner tower (Nano/Super via upstream Qwen3-VL support;
# the Edge tier's Nemotron-backbone reasoner via its dedicated integration).
# vLLM brings its own pinned torch/CUDA stack — that is the whole reason this
# venv is isolated from the lerobot-pinned openral runtime.
# Pure-PyPI resolution (no --torch-backend): vLLM's torch dependency ships the
# CUDA runtime in its PyPI wheels, so no PyTorch index redirect is needed.
# ``--no-config`` is load-bearing, not tidiness. Without it uv applies the
# WORKSPACE's `[tool.uv] constraint-dependencies` from the repo root
# pyproject.toml — including `torchcodec<0.10` on x86_64 linux, which exists
# to keep torchcodec's ABI paired with the main env's torch 2.9.1. That
# constraint has no business here: this venv is isolated precisely so vLLM can
# bring its own torch. Leaked in, it capped x86_64 at vllm 0.24.0 (which
# predates the native Cosmos3 Edge model, vllm#48291) while aarch64 resolved
# 0.28.0 — so `cosmos3-edge` fell back to vLLM's Transformers path on x86 and
# crashed in `cosmos3_edge.get_rope_index` on every request. Same command
# without the flag silently reintroduces it.
#
# Regenerate the lock with:
#   uv pip compile tools/sidecar_requirements/cosmos3_reasoner.in \
#     --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --no-config \
#     -o tools/sidecar_requirements/cosmos3_reasoner.lock
#
# Pinned rather than floored: 0.28.0 is the release the aarch64 live tool call
# was validated on, and resolving it universally reproduces that exact
# environment (torch 2.13.0 + torchcodec 0.16.0) on every platform instead of
# floating x86 onto an untested newer vLLM. Raise it deliberately, with a
# live tick to back the bump.
vllm==0.28.0
